Yes, once I add it. By default Langfuse only gets our model calls, so I would log each e-mail as a step in the same trace. One trace per case would then show, in order:

- the supplier's opening quote and its attached documents as text;
- each of our e-mails with its term sheets and cited data, next to the model call that produced it;
- each supplier reply with its status, standing offer and how our arguments checked out;
- after the case ends, the score, the cost breakdown, the supplier's reasons in words and its back-office notes.

What it will not contain is anything the arena hides: the supplier's prompt, its floor, and the figures it masks as `…`.

You already have all of this on disk today, without Langfuse: every run writes the whole case to `agent/runs/<run_id>/sessions/<sid>.json`. Langfuse adds a browsable view that links each message to the model decision behind it, and lets teammates look without copying run folders around.

